+<LegalLayout title="Privacy Notice">
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news site. You can read articles without creating an account. Use a made-up username and a password you do not use elsewhere if you try the account forms.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account forms</h2>
+    <p>Sign-up and sign-in request only a username and password. No email address, real name, or marketing preference is required. Details are sent only when you submit, over HTTPS to the authentication service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/</code>, hosted on Google Cloud, to create an account or check your credentials. The service also receives connection information such as your IP address.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not write credentials or authentication tokens to cookies, local storage, or session storage. The password field is cleared after each completed request. Your browser or password manager may offer to remember credentials under your own settings.</p>
+    <p>The authentication service is separate from this site's code. Its credential storage, logging, retention, and deletion practices cannot be verified here. Do not submit sensitive or reused credentials to this demonstration.</p>
+
+    <h2>Scripts, fonts, and external content</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics or advertising scripts. Fonts use your device's installed typefaces, without contacting a font provider. No analytics or advertising consent is required because those scripts are not loaded.</p>
+    <p>Some articles and teasers include externally hosted images. Loading them sends a request, including your IP address, to the image host. The site sets a no-referrer policy so these requests do not include the referring page address.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading list and cookies</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article creates a server-side reading list associated with a session cookie. It stores article identifiers for the reading-list feature. The site does not initialize an empty reading list on ordinary page visits. Removing a saved article removes its identifier from that list; clearing site cookies disconnects your browser from its previous session but does not itself delete server-side data.</p>
+    <p>Some demonstration articles intentionally exercise browser behavior, including setting sample cookies for an article statistics request. These are separate from account details. This notice does not promise that every demonstration is free of cookies.</p>
+
+    <h2>Questions and limitations</h2>
+    <p>This demonstration does not provide an account deletion interface or a verified retention schedule. Consult the <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>site information</a> for its demonstration context. Do not treat the sample account service as a production account system.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
